# Scratch queue rows WO (plan_process_overhaul.md P2.1). Data: the queue table in scratch_queue.md is generated
# from this file (python3 tools/status_index.py). Format: tools/scratch_query/qrows.py docstring.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT feature_writeup/testing/rows/WO.qb RES [--section KEY] [--rows ID,...]

@@section 1
@@title SQ-WO Wise Oak: sleep loop, trust command, gifts, oak biomes, web block, 2026-11-09 ([wise_oak.md](../wise_oak.md) 4 and 8, TODO `mobs/tweaks #19`)
@@date 2026-11-09
@@jars creativeworldgen
@@sources feature_writeup/wise_oak.md
@@text
@@text Targets Creative Worldgen 20:25 (installed in `mods/`). Reads go through Creative Devtools' `/cdevtest` (`state`, `items`, `entities`) and `/pbot punch` since 2026-11-16; the probe `tools/scratch_query/wo_probe.js` (`/zwo`) is still copied for `zwo skip` (game-time skip) and SQ-WO-27's `zwo drops` lines, which `wo_judge.py gifts` reads, and Creative Devtools' perfBot (`pbot`). Each row has its own tree at the X in its commands; X is unique per row, so rows in one boot do not interfere. G and H stand far from the trees so they do not pick drops up (`pbot use` needs no reach).
@@text
@@text | Boot | World | Srv config (`qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/creativeworldgen-common.toml <section> <key> <value>`) | Rows |
@@text |---|---|---|---|
@@text | A1 | A | defaults | SQ-WO-01 to -13 (restart row -10 last, or run -11 to -13 first) |
@@text | A2 | A | `wise_oak`: `sleepDurationSeconds = 5`, `angerDurationSeconds = 5`, `angrySleepDurationSeconds = 5`; `wise_oak.gifts`: `chancePercent = 100`, `trustThreshold = 75` | SQ-WO-14 to -30 |
@@text | A3 | A | row's Group column | SQ-WO-31 |
@@text | A4 | A | row's Group column | SQ-WO-32 |
@@text | A5 | A | row's Group column | SQ-WO-33, -34 |
@@text | B | B fresh, worldgen | `config/mysticaloaktree-common.toml` `tree_rarity = 1` | SQ-WO-35, -36 |
@@text | S | A, under strace | defaults | SQ-WO-37 |
@@text
@@text Every boot: copy the probe, `forceload add 270 290 900 320`, and spawn G and H as in SQ-WO-01. A `\|` in a table cell is a plain `|`. Reading: `cdevtest state X Y Z` prints the block state and game time. Timers: `data get block X Y Z creativeworldgen_sleep_until` (or `_angry_until`). Trust: `wiseoak trust X Y Z G`. Not scriptable, so left to CQ rows: the push, faces, particles, dialogue, and the talk counter reset.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-WO-01 | boot, web block logged once, config defaults, probe answers
@group A1 (first)
@commands `bash tools/scratch_query/prep_srv.sh OUT wo A`; `cp tools/scratch_query/wo_probe.js OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_wo_probe.js`; boot; `forceload add 270 290 900 320`; `pbot spawn G 280 -60 280 minecraft:overworld survival`; `pbot spawn H 276 -60 280 minecraft:overworld survival`; `cdevtest state 310 -60 300`; grep the boot log and `OUT/srv/config/creativeworldgen-common.toml` (WO-15)
@pass `Wise Oak web lookups disabled` count == 1; no `wiseoak` line with `InjectionError` or `failed`; `[wise_oak]` 300, 30, 600; `[wise_oak.gifts]` 5.0, 75, list sizes 17, 14, 14, 30, counts 1, 1, 4, 16; `/cdevtest state` answers
@fails A failed inject crashes boot or leaves stock behaviour: compare the `@At` targets in `WiseOakTileMixin` with the jar. Probe error: fix `wo_probe.js`, see its header
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1109wo/b1_defaults.qb passed
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (?i)wiseoak.*(InjectionError|failed)
bootreject (?i)InvalidInjectionException.*wiseoak
shell test "$(grep -c 'Wise Oak web lookups disabled' logs/latest.log)" = 1 && echo "web block line once"
shell python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/wo_judge.py" toml config/creativeworldgen-common.toml 300 30 600 5.0 75 17 14 14 30 1 1 4 16
> forceload add 270 290 900 320
sleep 8
> pbot spawn G 280 -60 280 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot spawn H 276 -60 280 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> cdevtest state 310 -60 300
expect verb=state pos=310,-60,300 
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0

## SQ-WO-02 | trust command reads, writes, selector, per player
@group A1
@commands `setblock 320 -60 300 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak`; `wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 G`; `wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 G 80`; `wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 G`; `wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 @a[name=G] 50`; `wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 G`; `wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 H`; `data get block 320 -60 300 relationship` (WO-18)
@pass `Trust of G at .*: 0`; `Set trust of G at .* to 80`; `: 80`; `to 50`; `: 50`; H reads `: 0` and no record for H in the NBT; the G record shows trust 50
@fails `WiseOakCommand`, `creativeworldgen$setTrust`, or the block update at the end of `set`
@from batches/r1109wo/b1_defaults.qb
> setblock 320 -60 300 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak
> wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 G
> wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 G 80
> wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 G
> wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 @a[name=G] 50
> wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 G
> wiseoak trust 320 -60 300 H
> data get block 320 -60 300 relationship
sleep 1
expect Trust of G at .*: 0
expect Set trust of G at .* to 80
expect Trust of G at .*: 80
expect to 50
expect Trust of G at .*: 50
expect Trust of H at .*: 0
look data get line: one record (G) with trust 50, none for H

## SQ-WO-03 | trust command errors (r1109 fault: an offline server resolves any plain name; use a selector that matches nobody)
@group A1
@commands On air `wiseoak trust 330 -60 300 G 50`; `setblock 330 -60 300 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak`; `wiseoak trust 330 -60 300 G 101`; `wiseoak trust 330 -60 300 G -1`; `wiseoak trust 330 -60 300 Nobody123 50`; `wiseoak trust 99999 -60 99999 G 50`; `setblock 330 -60 300 minecraft:stone`; `wiseoak trust 330 -60 300 G 50` (WO-18)
@pass `No Wise Oak at that position` twice; value rejected above 100 and below 0; `That player does not exist`; `That position is not loaded`; no exception in the log
@fails Argument ranges or the block entity check in `WiseOakCommand.tree`
@from batches/r1113/rerun_a.qb passed
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 G 50
> setblock 30030 -60 30020 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 G 101
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 G -1
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 @a[name=Nobody123] 50
> wiseoak trust 99999 -60 99999 G 50
> setblock 30030 -60 30020 minecraft:stone
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 G 50
sleep 2
count No Wise Oak at that position == 2
expect (?i)integer must not be more than 100
expect (?i)integer must not be less than 0
expect No player was found|That player does not exist
expect That position is not loaded
reject Set trust of Nobody123
reject Exception
# row text: the queue's "That player does not exist" is for a name lookup; with the selector it is "No player was found"

## SQ-WO-04 | stays awake by day at the default random tick speed (r1109 ran at 300: tired-roll suspicion)
@group A1
@commands `time set noon`; `weather clear`; `setblock 340 -60 300 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak`; sleep 120; `cdevtest state 340 -60 300` (WO-01)
